nalyzing Liturgical Sections**\n\nI'm now methodically analyzing the liturgical sections: Prokeimenon, readings, litanies, Litiya, Aposticha, and dismissal prayers. I'm noting Prokeimenon tones, verse structures, and deacon cues precisely. I'm specifying \n<truncated 467 bytes>\n of the Theotokos, and the culminating prayers of St. Ephrem, St. Basil, Paul the Monk, and Antiochus. I'm also confirming the Psalm structures like Psalms 4, 6, 12, 24, 30, and 90.\n\n\n**Examining Matins Elements**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the *Matins* service, specifically detailing elements for the \"12 Gates\" maximalist standard. I'm focusing on the *Royal Psalms* and the *Hexapsalmos*. I will clarify \"God is the Lord\" with *Alleluia*, the appointed *Kathismata*, and *Sessional Hymns*, which will be documented for card five. For the *Polyeleos* I'm concentrating on Psalm 134, Psalm 135, hymns to the Theotokos. Next, I will begin detailing the Gospel readings.\n\n\n**Detailing Matins Progression**\n\nI'm now detailing the full *Matins* structure, moving from *Polyeleos* with its Psalms (134 & 135) to the *Megalynarion* and the Evlogitaria. I'm noting the *Hypakoe*, Gradual Hymns (*Anavathmoi*), and *Prokeimenon*. I'll map the *Matins* Gospel, especially its connection to the *Eothinon* Resurrection Gospel and Psalm 50. I will detail the Canon's Odes (1-8), emphasizing the Heirmoi and Katavasia, along with the precise composition. I am documenting the full maximalist \"card.\"\n\n\n**Mapping Matins Finishes**\n\nI'm now focusing on the conclusion of Matins, starting after Ode 6 with the Kontakion, and Ikos. I'm noting the Exapostilarion/Praises section, including *Eothinon*, saint hymns, and Theotokion hymns. I'm detailing the Great Doxology, and specific dismissal Troparion, along with the concluding Litanies. I'm also preparing to document \"Card 6,\" specifically *The Hours* service, including precise Psalm assignments.\n\n\n**Defining Hour Distribution**\n\nI'm now detailing the hour distribution for Sundays, feasts, patronal days, and saints' days. I'm noting specific verses, prayers like *Order my steps*, and prayers of St. Mardarius, St. Basil, and St. Ephrem during Lent. I'm documenting the precise structure of all four Hours, working towards defining \"Card 7,\" which documents the maximalist standard for the Divine Liturgy.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content","thinking"]}
