{"step_index":676,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:15:13Z","content":"I will write the complete reference document `.agents/references/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md` to permanently codify the canonical maximalist audit standard for all 7 digest cards.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Authoritative reference codifying the Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard across all 7 cards.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard\\n\\n> **Authority**: 2010 Lviv Typikon; Dolnytsky Typikon Parts I–V (1899); Ordo Celebrationis (1944/1996).  \\n> **Status**: Immutable Authoritative Standard for Service Rubrics Digest Cards.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Overview & Purpose\\nThis standard defines the **Canonical Maximalist Specification** for every card in the **Service Rubrics Digest**. A card is considered canonically complete and marked `PASS` if and only if it satisfies all required checkpoints below with zero omitted, summarized, or hallucinated rubrics.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Hierarchy of Canonical Authority (Rule 2)\\n1. **Ordo Celebrationis** (Rome, 1944 / 1996) — Primary standard for service choreography, entrances, litanies, and hierarchy.\\n2. **Dolnytsky Typikon Parts II–V** (Lviv, 1899) — Specific rubrics for the Daily Cycle (Pt. II), Menaion (Pt. III), Triodion (Pt. IV), and Pentecostarion (Pt. V).\\n3. **2010 Lviv Typikon** — The authoritative modern UGCC codification.\\n4. **Liturgicon & Horologion** — Verbatim prayers, litanies, and ordos.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Card-by-Card Maximalist Checkpoints\\n\\n### Card 1: General Info Card\\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I & II (Headers of all 20 Paradigms); Ordo Celebrationis §§ 1–24.*\\n\\n- [ ] **Date Grounding**: Formats Civil Date, Julian/Old Calendar Date, and Day of the Week.\\n- [ ] **Full Commemoration Title**: Unabbreviated official name and title of the commemorated feast/saint.\\n- [ ] **Dolnytsky Rank & Symbol**: Canonical Rank (1 to 7) and liturgical classification (Simple, 6 Stichera, Doxology, Polyeleos, Vigil, Great Feast).\\n- [ ] **Tone & Eothinon Cycle**: Octoechos Tone of the Week (1–8) and Matins Resurrection Gospel Eothinon number (1–11 on Sundays).\\n- [ ] **Liturgical Season**: Exact liturgical period (Octoechos, Triodion, Pentecostarion, Dormition/Nativity Fast).\\n- [ ] **Combination Formula**: Full Dolnytsky Part II heading formula (e.g., *\\\"Dolnytsky Part II, Case 2: Simple Weekday service combined with Saint without Polyeleos\\\"*).\\n- \n<truncated 8789 bytes>","Description":"\"Codify Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard in .agents/references/\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\augus\\\\OneDrive\\\\Documents\\\\Google Antigravity\\\\Projects\\\\Typikon Coded\\\\.agents\\\\references\\\\canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing canonical maximalist digest standard\"","toolSummary":"\"Writing canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
{"step_index":678,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:15:22Z","content":"I will write `canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md` into the artifact directory.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard reference document.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard\\n\\n> **Authority**: 2010 Lviv Typikon; Dolnytsky Typikon Parts I–V (1899); Ordo Celebrationis (1944/1996).  \\n> **Status**: Immutable Authoritative Standard for Service Rubrics Digest Cards.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Overview & Purpose\\nThis standard defines the **Canonical Maximalist Specification** for every card in the **Service Rubrics Digest**. A card is considered canonically complete and marked `PASS` if and only if it satisfies all required checkpoints below with zero omitted, summarized, or hallucinated rubrics.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Hierarchy of Canonical Authority (Rule 2)\\n1. **Ordo Celebrationis** (Rome, 1944 / 1996) — Primary standard for service choreography, entrances, litanies, and hierarchy.\\n2. **Dolnytsky Typikon Parts II–V** (Lviv, 1899) — Specific rubrics for the Daily Cycle (Pt. II), Menaion (Pt. III), Triodion (Pt. IV), and Pentecostarion (Pt. V).\\n3. **2010 Lviv Typikon** — The authoritative modern UGCC codification.\\n4. **Liturgicon & Horologion** — Verbatim prayers, litanies, and ordos.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Card-by-Card Maximalist Checkpoints\\n\\n### Card 1: General Info Card\\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I & II (Headers of all 20 Paradigms); Ordo Celebrationis §§ 1–24.*\\n\\n- [ ] **Date Grounding**: Formats Civil Date, Julian/Old Calendar Date, and Day of the Week.\\n- [ ] **Full Commemoration Title**: Unabbreviated official name and title of the commemorated feast/saint.\\n- [ ] **Dolnytsky Rank & Symbol**: Canonical Rank (1 to 7) and liturgical classification (Simple, 6 Stichera, Doxology, Polyeleos, Vigil, Great Feast).\\n- [ ] **Tone & Eothinon Cycle**: Octoechos Tone of the Week (1–8) and Matins Resurrection Gospel Eothinon number (1–11 on Sundays).\\n- [ ] **Liturgical Season**: Exact liturgical period (Octoechos, Triodion, Pentecostarion, Dormition/Nativity Fast).\\n- [ ] **Combination Formula**: Full Dolnytsky Part II heading formula (e.g., *\\\"Dolnytsky Part II, Case 2: Simple Weekday service combined with Saint without Polyeleos\\\"*).\\n- \n<truncated 8789 bytes>","Description":"\"Create canonical maximalist digest standard artifact\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\augus\\\\/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing canonical maximalist digest standard\"","toolSummary":"\"Writing canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
