{"step_index":692,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:16:07Z","content":"I will update `.agents/references/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md` in the artifact directory and copy it to the references library, expanding it to cover all 20 canonical non-Triodion cases and all N Triodion/Pentecostarion seasonal cases with a uniform data presentation.","thinking":"**Considering Uniform Applicability**\n\nI'm now contemplating whether the standard can be enhanced to apply universally across all twenty cases outside the triodia and the specific 'n' case within it. The key is ensuring a consistent data presentation, regardless of the card or day. This unified approach seems promising, offering clarity.\n\n\n**Expanding Uniformity's Scope**\n\nI'm expanding the scope, aiming for uniformity across all twenty cases, excluding the Triodia and the 'n' sub-case. My focus remains on ensuring a consistent data representation across the entire corpus. This approach seems logical, enhancing clarity.\n\n\n\n**Analyzing Case Diversity**\n\nNow, I'm analyzing how these diverse scenarios, especially cases 17 through 20, fit into the broader framework. I'm focusing on the afterfeast, the weekdays, Saturdays, and Sundays in both Lenten and Bright weeks as they relate to all 'n' cases within the Triodia. The core concept is seamless integration and a consistent format for each scenario to minimize any possible confusion.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Enhanced Universal Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard covering all 20 Paradigms and all Triodia cases with uniform data presentation.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard (Universal Edition)\\n\\n> **Authority**: 2010 Lviv Typikon; Dolnytsky Typikon Parts I–V (1899); Ordo Celebrationis (1944/1996).  \\n> **Scope**: Uniformly applicable to all 20 Non-Triodion Paradigms and all N Triodia Cases (Lenten Triodion & Pentecostarion).  \\n> **Goal**: 100% consistent data presentation across every card of any day, where every card deterministically evaluates to `PASS`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Hierarchy of Canonical Authority (Rule 2)\\n1. **Ordo Celebrationis** (Rome, 1944 / 1996) — Primary standard for service choreography, entrances, litanies, and hierarchy.\\n2. **Dolnytsky Typikon Parts II–V** (Lviv, 1899) — Specific rubrics for Daily Cycle (Pt. II), Menaion (Pt. III), Triodion (Pt. IV), and Pentecostarion (Pt. V).\\n3. **2010 Lviv Typikon** — The authoritative modern UGCC codification.\\n4. **Liturgicon & Horologion** — Verbatim prayers, litanies, and ordos.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Universal Data Presentation Schema for Every Card\\n\\nEvery service card generated in the **Service Rubrics Digest** MUST render in this exact 6-tier uniform structure:\\n\\n```\\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n│ [TIER 1] CARD HEADER & BADGES                                               │\\n│ • Service Title (e.g. \\\"DAILY VESPERS\\\", \\\"GREAT MATINS (ALL-NIGHT VIGIL)\\\")    │\\n│ • Appointed Vestment Color Badge & Fasting Rule Badge (if service-specific) │\\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\\n│ [TIER 2] OPENING & ENTRANCE CHOREOGRAPHY                                    │\\n│ • Opening Blessing & Psalmody (Psalm 103, Hexapsalmos, or Royal Office)     │\\\n<truncated 11122 bytes>","Description":"\"Codify Universal Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard in artifact directory\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\augus\\\\/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing Universal Maximalist Digest Standard\"","toolSummary":"\"Writing canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
