{"step_index":726,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:25:01Z","content":"### 1. The 26 General Formats Explained (Non-Triodion + Triodia)\n\nIn the Byzantine-Ruthenian typikal tradition codified by **Dolnytsky Parts I–V**, the entire liturgical universe resolves into **exactly 26 General Formats**:\n\n* **Formats 1–20**: The 20 General Non-Triodion Paradigms (*Dolnytsky Part II* — Octoechos & Menaion rank combinations).\n* **Formats 21–26**: The 6 General Triodia Seasonal Formats (*Dolnytsky Parts IV & V* — Moveable cycle combinations).\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        THE 26 GENERAL CANONICAL FORMATS                                │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ NON-TRIODION GENERAL FORMATS (Dolnytsky Part II)                                       │\n│ • FORMAT 01: Sunday + Simple Saint (7 Oct + 3 Saint)                                   │\n│ • FORMAT 02: Weekday + Simple Saint (3 Oct + 3 Saint)                                  │\n│ • FORMAT 03: Sunday + 2 Saints (4 Oct + 3 Saint A + 3 Saint B)                         │\n│ • FORMAT 04: Weekday + 2 Saints (3 Saint A + 3 Saint B)                                 │\n│ • FORMAT 05: Sunday + Saint on 6 / Doxology (4 Oct + 6 Saint)                          │\n│ • FORMAT 06: Weekday + Saint on 6 / Doxology (All 6 Saint)                             │\n│ • FORMAT 07: Sunday + Polyeleos Saint (4 Oct + 6 Saint)                                │\n│ • FORMAT 08: Weekday + Polyeleos Saint (All 8 Saint)                                   │\n│ • FORMAT 09: Sunday + Vigil Saint (3 Oct + 3 Litiya +\n<truncated 3714 bytes>\n | Canonical Standard (Format 02) | Audit Status | Action Required |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: | :--- |\n| **1. Kathisma** | `No kathisma is appointed.` | Monday evening Vespers takes **Kathisma 18** unless preceding day had a Vigil (*Dolnytsky Pt. I*). | `[GAP]` | Update Kathisma resolver to appoint Kathisma 18. |\n| **2. Lord, I Call Stichera** | `we sing 6 Stichera to the Saint` | **6 Stichera: 3 from the Octoechos + 3 from the Menaion** (*Dolnytsky Pt. II, Case 2*). | `[GAP]` | Discard hardcoded string; format dynamic JSON distribution. |\n| **3. Prokeimenon** | `Daily Prokeimenon, Tone IV: \"The Lord hears me...\"` | Monday evening Prokeimenon is Tone IV (*\"The Lord hears me when I cry out to Him\"*). | `[PASS]` | Correctly appointed. |\n| **4. Aposticha** | `3 daily Aposticha from Octoechos; Glory, Both now: Aposticha Theotokion` | 3 Octoechos Aposticha + Aposticha Theotokion. | `[PASS]` | Correctly appointed. |\n| **5. Dismissal Troparia** | `Troparion of St. Eutyches; Glory, Both now: Dismissal Theotokion in Tone IV` | Saint Troparion (Tone IV) + Dismissal Theotokion in Tone IV (*Dolnytsky Pt. II, Case 2*). | `[PASS]` | Tone IV matching is correct. |\n\n---\n\n### Next Step: Patch and Verify Card 2\nWe will update [vespers.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/digest/formatters/vespers.py) to dynamically format the exact `3 Octoechos + 3 Menaion` distribution and appoint Kathisma 18, then run pytest to bring **Card 2 to 100% PASS**!\n\n---\n### Summary of Work\n* Codified all **26 General Formats (Formats 1–26)** in [.agents/references/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/.agents/references/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md).\n* Completed the deep audit of **Card 2 (Daily Vespers)**, pinpointed the hardcoded branch in [vespers.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/digest/formatters/vespers.py), and prepared the patch.","thinking":"**Analyzing Conditional Logic**\n\nI've been examining the conditional logic in lines 33-35 of `digest/formatters/vespers.py`. Speci